{"k":"itf","t":"Inverse Trigonometric Functions","cls":"12","u":"Trigonometry","s":[["Domains, ranges, graphs",[{"q":"Domain and principal range of $\\sin^{-1}x$","f":"\\sin^{-1}:[-1,1]\\to\\left[-\\tfrac\\pi2,\\tfrac\\pi2\\right]","g":"y=asin(x) ; -1.6,1.6,-1.8,1.8"},{"q":"Domain and principal range of $\\cos^{-1}x$","f":"\\cos^{-1}:[-1,1]\\to[0,\\pi]","g":"y=acos(x) ; -1.6,1.6,-0.3,3.4"},{"q":"Domain and principal range of $\\tan^{-1}x$","f":"\\tan^{-1}:\\mathbb R\\to\\left(-\\tfrac\\pi2,\\tfrac\\pi2\\right)","g":"y=atan(x) ; -6,6,-1.8,1.8"},{"q":"Ranges of $\\cot^{-1}$, $\\sec^{-1}$, $\\csc^{-1}$","f":"\\cot^{-1}:\\mathbb R\\to(0,\\pi),\\quad\\sec^{-1}:|x|\\ge1\\to[0,\\pi]-\\{\\tfrac\\pi2\\},\\quad\\csc^{-1}:|x|\\ge1\\to[-\\tfrac\\pi2,\\tfrac\\pi2]-\\{0\\}","g":"y=pi/2-atan(x) ; -6,6,-0.3,3.4"},{"q":"Graphs of $\\sec^{-1}x$ and $\\csc^{-1}x$","f":"\\sec^{-1}x\\in[0,\\tfrac\\pi2)\\cup(\\tfrac\\pi2,\\pi],\\qquad\\csc^{-1}x\\in[-\\tfrac\\pi2,0)\\cup(0,\\tfrac\\pi2]","g":"y=acos(1/x) | y=asin(1/x) ; -5,5,-1.8,3.4"},{"q":"Graph of $\\tan^{-1}(\\tan x)$","f":"\\tan^{-1}(\\tan x)=x-n\\pi\\ \\ \\text{for } x\\in\\left(n\\pi-\\tfrac\\pi2,\\ n\\pi+\\tfrac\\pi2\\right)","g":"y=atan(tan(x)) ; -7,7,-2,2"},{"q":"$\\cos^{-1}(\\cos x)$ piecewise","f":"\\cos^{-1}(\\cos x)=\\begin{cases}-x,&-\\pi\\le x\\le0\\\\x,&0\\le x\\le\\pi\\\\2\\pi-x,&\\pi\\le x\\le2\\pi\\end{cases}"}]],["Properties",[{"q":"Composition identities","f":"\\sin(\\sin^{-1}x)=x\\ (|x|\\le1);\\qquad\\sin^{-1}(\\sin x)=x\\ \\left(|x|\\le\\tfrac\\pi2\\right)"},{"q":"Graph of $\\sin^{-1}(\\sin x)$","f":"\\sin^{-1}(\\sin x)=\\begin{cases}x,&-\\frac\\pi2\\le x\\le\\frac\\pi2\\\\\\pi-x,&\\frac\\pi2\\le x\\le\\frac{3\\pi}2\\\\x-2\\pi,&\\frac{3\\pi}2\\le x\\le\\frac{5\\pi}2\\end{cases}","n":"Saw-tooth, period $2\\pi$. $\\cos^{-1}(\\cos x)$ is a triangular wave between $0$ and $\\pi$; $\\tan^{-1}(\\tan x)=x-n\\pi$.","g":"y=asin(sin(x)) | y=acos(cos(x)) ; -7,7,-2,3.5"},{"q":"Negative arguments","f":"\\sin^{-1}(-x)=-\\sin^{-1}x,\\quad\\tan^{-1}(-x)=-\\tan^{-1}x,\\quad\\cos^{-1}(-x)=\\pi-\\cos^{-1}x,\\quad\\cot^{-1}(-x)=\\pi-\\cot^{-1}x"},{"q":"Reciprocal arguments","f":"\\sin^{-1}\\tfrac1x=\\csc^{-1}x,\\qquad\\tan^{-1}\\tfrac1x=\\begin{cases}\\cot^{-1}x,&x>0\\\\-\\pi+\\cot^{-1}x,&x<0\\end{cases}"},{"q":"Complementary sums","f":"\\sin^{-1}x+\\cos^{-1}x=\\frac\\pi2,\\quad\\tan^{-1}x+\\cot^{-1}x=\\frac\\pi2,\\quad\\sec^{-1}x+\\csc^{-1}x=\\frac\\pi2"},{"q":"Composition the other way","f":"\\cos(\\sin^{-1}x)=\\sqrt{1-x^2},\\quad\\tan(\\sin^{-1}x)=\\frac x{\\sqrt{1-x^2}},\\quad\\sin(\\tan^{-1}x)=\\frac x{\\sqrt{1+x^2}},\\quad\\cos(\\tan^{-1}x)=\\frac1{\\sqrt{1+x^2}}"},{"q":"Reciprocal for $\\cos^{-1}$, $\\sec^{-1}$","f":"\\cos^{-1}\\frac1x=\\sec^{-1}x\\ (|x|\\ge1),\\qquad\\cot^{-1}\\frac1x=\\tan^{-1}x\\ (x>0)"},{"q":"Negative of $\\sec^{-1}$, $\\csc^{-1}$","f":"\\sec^{-1}(-x)=\\pi-\\sec^{-1}x,\\qquad\\csc^{-1}(-x)=-\\csc^{-1}x"},{"q":"$\\cot^{-1}x$ for negative $x$ in terms of $\\tan^{-1}$","f":"\\cot^{-1}x=\\begin{cases}\\tan^{-1}\\frac1x,&x>0\\\\\\pi+\\tan^{-1}\\frac1x,&x<0\\end{cases}"}]],["Sum and difference",[{"q":"Sum of inverse tangents","f":"\\tan^{-1}x+\\tan^{-1}y=\\begin{cases}\\tan^{-1}\\frac{x+y}{1-xy},&xy<1\\\\\\pi+\\tan^{-1}\\frac{x+y}{1-xy},&x,y>0,\\ xy>1\\\\-\\pi+\\tan^{-1}\\frac{x+y}{1-xy},&x,y<0,\\ xy>1\\end{cases}","n":"$xy=1$, $x>0$: sum $=\\frac\\pi2$."},{"q":"Difference of inverse tangents","f":"\\tan^{-1}x-\\tan^{-1}y=\\tan^{-1}\\frac{x-y}{1+xy}\\quad(xy>-1)"},{"q":"Sum of inverse sines","f":"\\sin^{-1}x+\\sin^{-1}y=\\sin^{-1}\\left(x\\sqrt{1-y^2}+y\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\right)","n":"Valid when $x,y\\ge0$ and $x^2+y^2\\le1$ (other cases add/subtract $\\pi$)."},{"q":"Sum of inverse cosines","f":"\\cos^{-1}x+\\cos^{-1}y=\\cos^{-1}\\left(xy-\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\sqrt{1-y^2}\\right)\\quad(x+y\\ge0)"},{"q":"Three inverse tangents","f":"\\tan^{-1}x+\\tan^{-1}y+\\tan^{-1}z=\\tan^{-1}\\frac{x+y+z-xyz}{1-xy-yz-zx}"},{"q":"Difference of inverse sines","f":"\\sin^{-1}x-\\sin^{-1}y=\\sin^{-1}\\left(x\\sqrt{1-y^2}-y\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\right)\\quad(xy\\ge0\\ \\text{or}\\ x^2+y^2\\le1)"},{"q":"Difference of inverse cosines","f":"\\cos^{-1}x-\\cos^{-1}y=\\cos^{-1}\\left(xy+\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\sqrt{1-y^2}\\right)\\quad(x\\le y)"},{"q":"Sum of inverse cotangents","f":"\\cot^{-1}x+\\cot^{-1}y=\\cot^{-1}\\frac{xy-1}{x+y}\\quad(x,y>0)"},{"q":"General $n$ inverse tangents","f":"\\sum\\tan^{-1}x_i=\\tan^{-1}\\frac{S_1-S_3+S_5-\\cdots}{1-S_2+S_4-\\cdots}","n":"$S_k$ = sum of products of the $x_i$ taken $k$ at a time."}]],["Multiple angles",[{"q":"$2\\tan^{-1}x$ forms","f":"2\\tan^{-1}x=\\sin^{-1}\\frac{2x}{1+x^2}\\ (|x|\\le1)=\\cos^{-1}\\frac{1-x^2}{1+x^2}\\ (x\\ge0)=\\tan^{-1}\\frac{2x}{1-x^2}\\ (|x|<1)"},{"q":"$2\\sin^{-1}x$ and $2\\cos^{-1}x$","f":"2\\sin^{-1}x=\\sin^{-1}\\left(2x\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\right)\\ \\left(|x|\\le\\tfrac1{\\sqrt2}\\right),\\qquad2\\cos^{-1}x=\\cos^{-1}(2x^2-1)\\ (0\\le x\\le1)"},{"q":"Triple forms","f":"3\\sin^{-1}x=\\sin^{-1}(3x-4x^3),\\quad3\\cos^{-1}x=\\cos^{-1}(4x^3-3x),\\quad3\\tan^{-1}x=\\tan^{-1}\\frac{3x-x^3}{1-3x^2}","n":"Valid on the restricted intervals $|x|\\le\\frac12$ (for sin, tan: $|x|<\\frac1{\\sqrt3}$), $\\frac12\\le x\\le1$ for cos."},{"q":"$2\\tan^{-1}x$ outside $|x|\\le1$","f":"2\\tan^{-1}x=\\pi-\\sin^{-1}\\frac{2x}{1+x^2}\\ (x>1),\\qquad-\\pi-\\sin^{-1}\\frac{2x}{1+x^2}\\ (x<-1)"},{"q":"$2\\sin^{-1}x$ outside the basic range","f":"2\\sin^{-1}x=\\pi-\\sin^{-1}\\left(2x\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\right)\\ \\left(\\tfrac1{\\sqrt2}<x\\le1\\right)"},{"q":"$\\cos^{-1}\\frac{1-x^2}{1+x^2}$ for negative $x$","f":"\\cos^{-1}\\frac{1-x^2}{1+x^2}=-2\\tan^{-1}x\\quad(x\\le0)"}]],["Conversions",[{"q":"Converting between inverse functions","f":"\\sin^{-1}x=\\cos^{-1}\\sqrt{1-x^2}=\\tan^{-1}\\frac x{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\\quad(0\\le x<1)","h":"Draw a right triangle with opposite $x$, hypotenuse $1$."},{"q":"$\\cos^{-1}x$ in other forms","f":"\\cos^{-1}x=\\sin^{-1}\\sqrt{1-x^2}=\\tan^{-1}\\frac{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}x\\quad(0<x\\le1)"},{"q":"$\\tan^{-1}x$ in other forms","f":"\\tan^{-1}x=\\sin^{-1}\\frac x{\\sqrt{1+x^2}}=\\cos^{-1}\\frac1{\\sqrt{1+x^2}}\\quad(x\\ge0)"}]],["Common results",[{"q":"Telescoping inverse tangent sums","f":"\\tan^{-1}\\frac{1}{1+r(r+1)}=\\tan^{-1}(r+1)-\\tan^{-1}r","n":"General trick: write $\\frac{x-y}{1+xy}$ form. $\\sum_{r=1}^\\infty\\tan^{-1}\\frac1{2r^2}=\\frac\\pi4$."},{"q":"Useful values","f":"\\tan^{-1}1+\\tan^{-1}2+\\tan^{-1}3=\\pi,\\qquad\\tan^{-1}\\tfrac12+\\tan^{-1}\\tfrac13=\\tfrac\\pi4"},{"q":"Sum of $\\sin^{-1}$ constraint","f":"\\sin^{-1}x+\\sin^{-1}y+\\sin^{-1}z=\\frac{3\\pi}2\\Rightarrow x=y=z=1","n":"Similar extreme-value tricks: $\\cos^{-1}x+\\cos^{-1}y+\\cos^{-1}z=3\\pi\\Rightarrow x=y=z=-1$."},{"q":"Standard simplifications","f":"\\tan^{-1}\\sqrt{\\frac{1-\\cos x}{1+\\cos x}}=\\frac x2\\ (0<x<\\pi),\\qquad\\tan^{-1}\\frac{\\cos x}{1+\\sin x}=\\frac\\pi4-\\frac x2"},{"q":"$\\tan^{-1}\\frac{\\cos x-\\sin x}{\\cos x+\\sin x}$","f":"=\\frac\\pi4-x\\quad\\left(-\\tfrac\\pi4<x<\\tfrac{3\\pi}4\\right)"},{"q":"$\\sin^{-1}\\frac{2x}{1+x^2}+\\cos^{-1}\\frac{1-x^2}{1+x^2}$ type values","f":"4\\tan^{-1}x\\ (0\\le x\\le1)"},{"q":"Solving inverse trig equations","f":"\\text{take } \\sin/\\cos/\\tan \\text{ of both sides; check every root against the principal ranges}"},{"q":"Inverse trig inequalities","f":"\\sin^{-1}x>\\cos^{-1}x\\iff x\\in\\left(\\tfrac1{\\sqrt2},1\\right];\\qquad\\tan^{-1}x>\\cot^{-1}x\\iff x>1"},{"q":"Sum of the series $\\sum\\tan^{-1}\\frac{2}{n^2}$ / $\\sum\\cot^{-1}(n^2+n+1)$","f":"\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty\\cot^{-1}(n^2+n+1)=\\frac\\pi4,\\qquad\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty\\tan^{-1}\\frac2{n^2}=\\frac{3\\pi}4"}]],["If this type comes, solve like this",[{"q":"If it is $\\sum\\cot^{-1}(\\text{quadratic in } n)$ or $\\sum\\tan^{-1}$ — a telescoping sum","f":"\\cot^{-1}\\frac{1+ab}{a-b}=\\tan^{-1}a-\\tan^{-1}b","n":"Write the term as $\\tan^{-1}\\frac{x_{n+1}-x_n}{1+x_nx_{n+1}}$ (e.g. $1+n(n+1)$ in the denominator ⇒ $\\tan^{-1}(n+1)-\\tan^{-1}n$). Sum telescopes; infinite sums tend to $\\frac\\pi2-\\tan^{-1}(\\text{first})$.","p":"3 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 11 times"},{"q":"If it asks $\\sin^{-1}(\\sin\\theta)$, $\\cos^{-1}(\\cos\\theta)$, $\\tan^{-1}(\\tan\\theta)$ for $\\theta$ outside the principal range","f":"\\sin^{-1}(\\sin\\theta)=\\pi-\\theta\\ \\left(\\tfrac\\pi2\\le\\theta\\le\\tfrac{3\\pi}2\\right),\\ \\ \\theta-2\\pi\\ \\ldots;\\quad\\cos^{-1}(\\cos\\theta)=2\\pi-\\theta\\ (\\pi\\le\\theta\\le2\\pi)","n":"Shift $\\theta$ by multiples of $2\\pi$ (or $\\pi$ for tan) into the principal range, using the graph's saw-tooth/triangle shape.","h":"Trap: $\\cos^{-1}(\\cos(-5))=2\\pi-5$, $\\sin^{-1}(\\sin6)=6-2\\pi$, $\\tan^{-1}(\\tan12)=12-4\\pi$.","p":"3 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 6 times"},{"q":"If it asks the value of a trig function of a combination of inverse functions","f":"\\text{convert each to one function using a right triangle, then use } \\tan(A+B),\\ \\sin2A\\ \\ldots","n":"$2\\cot^{-1}5=\\tan^{-1}\\frac{2\\cdot\\frac15}{1-\\frac1{25}}$; $\\cos^{-1}\\frac45=\\tan^{-1}\\frac34$.","p":"7 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 19 times"},{"q":"If it is an equation in inverse trig functions","f":"\\tan^{-1}x+\\cot^{-1}x=\\tfrac\\pi2,\\ \\ \\sin^{-1}x+\\cos^{-1}x=\\tfrac\\pi2;\\ \\ \\text{take tan/sin/cos of both sides}","n":"1) Reduce to one function. 2) Take a trig function of both sides. 3) Solve; reject roots that violate the principal ranges or the $xy<1$ condition of the $\\tan^{-1}$ sum formula.","p":"8 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 21 times"},{"q":"If it asks the domain of $\\sin^{-1}(g(x))$ / $\\cos^{-1}(g(x))$ with other terms","f":"-1\\le g(x)\\le1\\ \\ \\text{(solve both inequalities)};\\ \\ \\sec^{-1}:\\ |g|\\ge1","p":"5 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 10 times"},{"q":"If it asks the range of $(\\tan^{-1}x)^3+(\\cot^{-1}x)^3$ or similar","f":"\\text{put } t=\\tan^{-1}x\\in\\left(-\\tfrac\\pi2,\\tfrac\\pi2\\right),\\ \\cot^{-1}x=\\tfrac\\pi2-t","n":"Expand: a quadratic in $t$; find its range on the open interval.","p":"1 PYQ (2019–2026) · asked 5 times"},{"q":"If a $\\sin^{-1}$ argument is $a\\cos+b\\sin$ form like $\\frac{\\sqrt3}2x+\\frac12\\sqrt{1-x^2}$","f":"x=\\sin\\theta\\Rightarrow\\sin\\left(\\theta+\\tfrac\\pi6\\right)\\Rightarrow\\text{answer}=\\tfrac\\pi6+\\sin^{-1}x\\ \\text{(within range)}","p":"1 PYQ (2019–2026) · asked 3 times"},{"q":"If inverse trig is mixed with calculus/series","f":"f'(x)=\\tan^{-1}(\\sec x+\\tan x)=\\frac\\pi4+\\frac x2\\ \\text{(simplify first)}","n":"Also: $\\tan^{-1}a+\\tan^{-1}b=\\frac\\pi4\\Rightarrow(1+a)(1+b)=2$, so $\\ln(1+a)+\\ln(1+b)=\\ln2$.","p":"3 PYQs (2019–2026) · asked 4 times"}]]]}